==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuthRequired lets the model invent a granted operation with no upstream authentication; the injection forces exactly such an operation and the assertion that 'granted implies authenticated' must fail.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilegeEnforcement  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_LeastPrivilegeEnforcement.als
    rationale: Removing the matrix-lookup fact lets a role escalate beyond its permitted operation kinds. The injection forces an auditor-only caller to be granted POST /applications, which the permission matrix forbids.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAppendOnly  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AuditAppendOnly.als
    rationale: Removing the per-(application, newStatus) uniqueness lets the model record two distinct audit entries for the same logical transition, which is exactly the duplication an append-only log forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_018_AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccessEnforcement  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccessEnforcement.als
    rationale: Without the ownership filter, a granted GET /applications/{id} can land on a caller who is neither the applicant, the assigned officer, nor an auditor — leaking another customer's application.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_012_OnlyAssignedOfficerPatches
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_OnlyAssignedOfficerPatches: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_NoSelfAssignment  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoSelfAssignment.als
    rationale: Removing the disjointness between an application's applicant and its assigned officer lets a user be auto-assigned to their own application, which is the structural precondition the self-decision rule defends against.
    expected to FAIL: NoSelfMutation, FR_011_NoSelfAssignment, OwnershipExclusivity
      - NoSelfMutation: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_011_NoSelfAssignment: PASS (vacuous?)
      - OwnershipExclusivity: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_NoInformationLeakageEnforcement  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoInformationLeakageEnforcement.als
    rationale: Removing the canonical-response rule lets a denied authenticated GET return ForbiddenResp instead of the byte-equivalent NotFoundResp, leaking existence of another customer's application.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_020_ByteEquivNotFound
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_020_ByteEquivNotFound: PASS (vacuous?)

